      "author": "preseen-human",
      "created_at": "2026-10-14",
      "text": "@(johnnycaffeine)Thanks for the clarification. Is it fair to assume that a secret service detail dispatched in advance of the President or other cabinet officer to ensure a polling place was safe wouldn't resolve this question? Would it make any difference how the secret service detail behaved (i.e. if did anything else besides playing a clearly protective role)?"
    },
    {
      "author": "DaiLothbrook",
      "created_at": "2026-10-12",
      "text": "iN THis first estimate, so far, I will  assign 5% to a qualifying deployment. Reports of agents near voting activity and preparations by election officials make me less comfortable with my initial 2% prior, but proximity and rhetoric are not the same as an order placing armed personnel at a polling or early-voting site. DHS says it has no plan for broad ICE patrols, and legal barriers are substantial. The biggest uncertainty is what Metaculus IS REQUIRING   as proof of a governor- or administration-directed deployment. Sources: [AP](https://www.ap.org/news-highlights/elections/2026/trump-administration-says-it-has-no-plans-for-ice-officers-at-polls-activists-are-preparing-anyway/), [Axios](https://www.axios.com/2026/09/17/states-ice-polls-2026-election), [Brennan Center](https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/federal-and-state-election-laws-ban-federal-forces-polling-places)."
    },
    {
      "author": "johnnycaffeine",
      "created_at": "2026-10-12",
      "text": "@(ChaosCondensate) Thank you for the question. If the ICE officers were specifically sent to the polling site to execute the warrant, and in-person voting were underway at the time, that would seem to be consistent with a deliberate deployment."
    },
    {
      "author": "ChaosCondensate",
      "created_at": "2026-10-12",
      "text": "@(admins) how strictly should \"deliberately deployed\" be read? Concrete case: armed ICE officers enter a building to make an arrest on a warrant unrelated to the election, while in-person early voting for the 2026general election is underway inside that same building, and they are within 250 feet of the entrance. Does that resolve YES, or is it excluded as incidental to their other duties? Thank you"
    }
